Roehub OpenBao 2.5.4 licensed QR derivative
================================================

This image is a modified build of OpenBao 2.5.4.

OpenBao source:
- repository: https://github.com/openbao/openbao
- tag: v2.5.4
- revision: 4f6d47246a053375271a5fd8af85c3b75695aa46
- archive: https://github.com/openbao/openbao/archive/refs/tags/v2.5.4.tar.gz
- archive SHA-256: f4ed87e3b6ec213e3aada0b4eba3ce1a9525620b14a0dde5be4de0c778be0291
- license: MPL-2.0

Roehub modification:
- patch: infra/docker/openbao/openbao-2.5.4-licensed-qr.patch
- purpose: preserve JWT-authentication terminal QR output while removing
  github.com/yeqown/reedsolomon@v1.0.0, whose source archive has no license.
- reproducibility: rename the unchanged flash-messages service source from
  .ts to .js so Ember has one deterministic extension for that module, and
  assign fixed semantic IDs to the three generated ember-auto-import modules
  instead of hashing Broccoli's per-build temporary directory path; generated
  JavaScript and CSS assets are named from their content rather than Webpack's
  transient chunk graph, and the service worker cache key uses the fixed
  project version instead of the current time and a random value.

Licensed replacement:
- module: github.com/skip2/go-qrcode
- version: v0.0.0-20200617195104-da1b6568686e
- revision: da1b6568686e89143e94f980a98bc2dbd5537f13
- source: https://github.com/skip2/go-qrcode/tree/da1b6568686e89143e94f980a98bc2dbd5537f13
- license: MIT
- license SHA-256: 4cdab772de606bdf53e174b2f5d6a2c398156380ca1f763122198cece531d02c

The complete modified OpenBao source, this patch, and the replacement module
source must accompany a distributable Roehub offline release. The image embeds
the full MPL-2.0 and MIT license texts under /licenses.

Runtime package layers:
- source image: ghcr.io/openbao/openbao:2.5.4
- source image index: sha256:436eaf9778cad75507ff70ea26ace30dcbe15606e619ac3823495663d7f7c115
- linux/amd64 package layer: sha256:3e26a337cf92c8ca21797fbf622f27b9b492f2e74d9a5af980190330fa733b8f
- linux/arm64 package layer: sha256:a537d976b5ef3dfae7ea89f86494c71a2ce077b6c22dbf077f6f2d4dc3586196

Only the upstream Alpine package-install layers are reused. They contain
libcap, su-exec, dumb-init and tzdata plus the matching APK database. They do
not contain OpenBao binaries or Go modules. This keeps the runtime package set
digest-pinned without consulting a mutable Alpine package index during build.
